        "AbstractText": {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "AIMS",
          "content": "Sudden cardiac death (SCD) is frequently caused by ventricular fibrillation (VF) occurring in the course of acute myocardial infarction (AMI). It has not been investigated yet, to what extent markers of coagulation activation and inflammation differ between patients with and without VF in the acute phase of AMI."
        }
